# Shared UI lives in platform-ui (required)

Every reusable presentational / layout / form / feedback component for product apps belongs in:

`packages/platform-ui` → import from `@companyio/platform-ui`

## Do this

- Add new shared UI under `packages/platform-ui/src/components/ui/` (or existing form/layout folders when that matches the pattern).
- Export it from `packages/platform-ui/src/index.tsx`.
- Rebuild the package (`pnpm --filter @companyio/platform-ui build`) before apps consume new exports.
- Apps (`web`, `admin`, `desktop`, …) only **compose** these primitives in `features/` / `pages/`.

## Do not do this

- Do **not** create `apps/*/src/ui/` for shared page shells, toasts, buttons, tables, dialogs, date pickers, form fields, etc.
- Do **not** duplicate `DataTable`, `FormField`, `ConfirmDialog`, `DatePicker`, `Modal`, `PageShell`, `toast`, action button classes, etc. inside an app.
- Do **not** put reusable UI under `apps/*/src/components` unless it is truly one-app-only and cannot be shared — prefer platform-ui by default.

## Already in platform-ui (use these)

- Forms: `FormField`, `Input`, `Label`, `Select`, `DatePicker`, …
- Feedback: `ConfirmDialog`, `useConfirmDialog`, `toast`, `AppToaster`, `Notice`, `Alert`, …
- Data: `DataTable`, …
- Layout / page chrome: `PageShell`, `PageHeader`, `Surface`, `SurfaceHeader`, `KpiCard`, `LiveBadge`, `QuickAction`, `primaryActionClass`, `secondaryActionClass`, `submitActionLabel`, `ActionSpinner`, …

## When finishing UI work

1. New shared piece → platform-ui + export + build  
2. App imports from `@companyio/platform-ui` only  
3. No leftover local copy under the app
